WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
This demonstration uses real Oracle and Bedrock
services with three synthetic policies.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Titan creates embeddings, Oracle retrieves
evidence, and Nova generates a cited answer.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
The application is local; the database and model
calls run in the cloud.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
The Python code invokes Titan Text Embeddings
version two through the AWS SDK.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
It requests one thousand twenty-four dimensions
and validates the returned vector.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
The same embedding model processes every
document and each new question.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.000
This is the SQL actually executed by the live
demonstration.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Bound documents become vectors; Oracle orders
them by exact cosine distance.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.000
A temporary CLOB holds the large payload. No
persistent tables are changed.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
This capture shows the result returned by the
live browser application.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
The transfer policy ranks first and supplies the
thirty-seven-hour approval requirement.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.000
The evidence text and distance are visible, so
you can inspect the citation.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
The sensor warranty question retrieves a
different document as the top result.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Its eighteen-month answer is supported by the
displayed warranty policy.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Each click calls the services again; these are
not prewritten application answers.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Project Aspen has no policy in this deliberately
small document fixture.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Inspect the live response instead of accepting a
borrowed policy for another project.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.000
This example is a useful check, not a
comprehensive hallucination evaluation.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Configure private database settings, sign into
AWS, and run the smoke test.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Start the browser app and select one of the four
bounded policy questions.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.000
Quick and EKS remain blocked by account
permissions, not proven by this RAG demo.
